.TH TECHNE 1 "2026-10-06" "techne 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
\&
.PP
techne \- operate Knowledge Islands Techne Harness
.SH SYNOPSIS
\&
.TP
.B techne
.RI [ global-options ]
.I command
.TP
.B techne completion bash|zsh
Print a completion definition for the selected shell.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&
.B techne
is the operator command-line interface for the Techne controller
execution fabric.
It keeps provider credentials out of command arguments and enforces the
configured AWS account boundary before controller and agent host operations.
Hosts are named by binding files and built from harness recipes; the
controller is the provider table in
.BR config.toml .
There are no built-in targets.
.SH COMMANDS
\&
.TP
.B diag
Report share-safe tool/version, local/release/unknown installation mode,
executing host platform and architecture, runtime/version, and effective
configuration presence without network access.
Local identifiers are redacted unless
.B --full
is supplied; review full output before sharing it.
Local provenance requires a resolved development checkout matching this tool's
source/package layout and a Git checkout or worktree marker. Copied source
without that evidence reports unknown; a source URL alone is insufficient.
.TP
.B help [command]
Show general help, or help for a command or command group such as
.BR host .
.TP
.B doctor
Check the local runtime and the configured controller target, then its
provider's tools and identity; with no controller table the controller checks
are skipped.
Show the same diagnostic context, read-only scope, healthy/unhealthy verdict,
and pass/warn/fail/skipped counts. Identity may contact AWS but never changes
provider state; unavailable prerequisite checks report actionable failures and
dependent identity checks are explicitly skipped. Numeric account identities
and raw provider errors are omitted. Health does not imply package freshness.
.TP
.B auth login
Reconcile authentication surfaces declared by the effective Techne
configuration with supported provider clients installed locally. The current
configuration declares AWS only. A valid session is retained; a recognised
expired IAM Identity Center session opens an interactive AWS SSO login and
then revalidates the expected account. Missing clients, unsupported profiles
and non-authentication failures do not trigger login.
JSON output and non-interactive terminals are not supported for this command.
.TP
.B controller status
Report the configured controller CloudFormation stack and controller
instance.
.TP
.B controller bootstrap
Open a private interactive Session Manager bootstrap session on the
controller.
JSON output is not supported for this interactive command.
.TP
.B recipe list
List the recipes in the harness checkout and the providers each supports,
marking the selected host's recipe.
.TP
.B recipe show [recipe]
Show a recipe's parameters and providers; without an argument, the selected
host's recipe.
.TP
.B host list
List the host bindings with their recipe and provider, marking the selected
host and how it was selected.
.TP
.B host add \fIname\fP --recipe \fIrecipe\fP [--provider \fIprovider\fP]
Write
.BI hosts/ name .toml
with one empty provider table for the recipe.
.B --provider
is required when the recipe supports more than one provider.
Refuses to overwrite and provisions nothing.
.TP
.B host status [--all]
Report the selected host's instance and state through its provider, without
changing it. When the instance is running, also run the recipe's status
script from the harness checkout and print its workspace report unchanged;
JSON output carries it in a
.B workspace
object.
.B --all
reports every binding and cannot be combined with
.B --host
or provider options.
A failed workspace report or binding exits 1 after the report.
.TP
.B host setup --host \fIname\fP [--pull]
Check that Tailscale reaches the host, then run the recipe's setup script
from the harness checkout to converge the host workspace over SSH.
.B --pull
fast-forwards clean checkouts on the host.
.TP
.B host start --host \fIname\fP
Start a stopped host and wait until it runs.
.TP
.B host stop --host \fIname\fP
Stop a running host.
.TP
.B host teardown --host \fIname\fP
Terminate the host after the instance identifier is typed at an
interactive prompt, then list the recipe footprint still to remove.
This cannot be undone.
.TP
.B host connect [path]
Check that Tailscale reaches the selected host, then open
.I path
(default home) in Zed over SSH. Makes no AWS call.
.PP
Host commands act on one host binding, selected by
.BR --host ,
then
.BR TECHNE_HOST ,
then
.B default_host
in
.BR config.toml ,
then the only binding. A name that is not a binding is an error at every step.
.BR setup ,
.BR start ,
.B stop
and
.B teardown
change a host and require
.B --host
even when another step would select one.
AWS host commands refuse credentials that are not the recipe's operator role
in the expected account, and refuse unless exactly one instance matches the
recipe's selectors.
.BR setup ,
.BR start ,
.BR stop ,
.B teardown
and
.B connect
accept
.BR --dry-run .
The
.B setup
and
.B connect
commands make no AWS call.
.TP
.B completion bash|zsh
Print a sourceable Bash or Zsh completion definition to standard output.
The installer does not alter shell startup files or completion directories.
.SH COMPLETION
\&
.PP
For the current Bash session, run
.BR "source <(techne completion bash)" .
For Zsh, write
.B techne completion zsh
to an
.B _techne
file in a directory on
.B fpath
before running
.BR compinit .
Keep persistent activation in shell configuration or a configuration manager.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
\&
.TP
.BI "--host " name
Select the host binding. Required by
.BR "host setup" ,
.BR start ,
.B stop
and
.BR teardown .
.TP
.BI "--harness-dir " path
Select the local ki-techne-harness checkout holding the recipes and host
scripts. Defaults to
.BR $HOME/workspaces/kit/knowledgeislands/ki-techne-harness .
.TP
.B --all
Report every host binding, for
.BR "host status" .
.TP
.BI "--recipe " recipe
Recipe for
.BR "host add" .
.TP
.BI "--provider " provider
Provider for
.BR "host add" ,
when the recipe supports several.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print host changes without making them.
.TP
.B --pull
Fast-forward clean checkouts on the host during
.BR "host setup" .
.TP
.B --json
Request machine-readable output where supported.
.TP
.B --full
Include local paths and identifiers in diagnostic output.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show help for the selected command or command group; a command group given
without a command is a usage error.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Show the version.
.SH PROVIDER OPTIONS
\&
.PP
Provider options apply only to a command whose target, the selected host or
the controller, uses that provider; anything else is a usage error.
Each overrides the binding or controller table value.
.TP
.BI "--aws-profile " name
AWS profile for the target; for a host, the admin profile its scripts use.
Falls back to the table value, then
.BR AWS_PROFILE .
.TP
.BI "--aws-region " region
AWS region. Falls back to the table value, then
.BR AWS_REGION .
.TP
.BI "--aws-account " id
Expected AWS account identifier.
.TP
.BI "--aws-controller-stack " name
Controller CloudFormation stack; controller only.
.TP
.BI "--aws-operator-profile " name
AWS profile for the host operator role; host only.
.SH FILES
\&
.TP
.B ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/techne/config.toml
Optional
.B default_host
and at most one
.BI [controller. provider ]
table, such as
.BR [controller.aws] .
.TP
.BI ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/techne/hosts/ name .toml
One host binding: schema
.BR techne/host-binding/v1 ,
.BR name ,
.BR recipe ,
optional recipe parameters and exactly one provider table, such as
.BR [aws] .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
\&
.TP
.B TECHNE_HOST
Host binding to select when
.B --host
is absent.
.TP
.B AWS_PROFILE
AWS profile when neither option nor table sets one.
.TP
.B AWS_REGION
AWS region when neither option nor table sets one.
.TP
.B TECHNE_HARNESS_DIR
Default ki-techne-harness checkout.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base of the configuration directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
\&
.PP
Returns 0 on success, 1 on operational or health-check failure and 2 on
invalid command usage.
.SH SECURITY
\&
.PP
Never place credentials, provider sessions, numeric operator identifiers
or raw Telegram updates in command arguments, Git or retained evidence.
.SH SEE ALSO
\&
.TP
.BR aws (1)
